// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row mutex_rwlock_raii_guard_refused (tier 3, `refuses`). Rust-parity audit 2026-09-26 (medium): Mutex/RwLock have no RAII guard: lock() is unsafe and returns *mut T with manual unlock
// Logos: Rust's `m.lock().unwrap()` guard spelling is refused; the only API is all-unsafe returning raw *mut T with manual .unlock(); no guard object, no Result/poisoning, no auto-unlock on scope exit or panic
// rustc: compiles, exits 0, fully safe RAII surface
// fix hint: stdlib logos.lcm.sync: MutexGuard/RwLockReadGuard/RwLockWriteGuard with Deref/DerefMut + Drop unlock; lock() -> LockResult<Guard>.
package mutex_rwlock_raii_guard_refused;
use logos.lcm.sync;
fn main() -> i32 {
    let m: Mutex<i32> = mutex_new::<i32>(10);
    {
        let mut g = m.lock().unwrap();
        *g = *g + 5;
    }
    let v = *m.lock().unwrap();
    return v - 15;
}
